window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY=window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY||{};window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY["tutorial-smoke-stall-20261005.en"]=[{"body": "# Tutorial compatibility smoke stall investigation\n\n> **2026-10-28 A2 correction:** References to the large edict window, ≡ menu and their dedicated components or smokes are historical. Use the [current entry points](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs) and [replacement screens and source owners](Hunt_Edict_Window_Removal_20261028.en.md). Earlier captures and test counts describe the earlier implementation.\n\nUpdated: 2026-10-05 · [한국어](Tutorial_Smoke_Stall_20261005.md)\n\nThe second launch of `-hellscriptTutorialSmoke` (`-hellscriptTutorialResume`) was reported to fail after about 170 s with `Timed out following the prologue gate: survival lesson target=`, on `origin/main` at `ee5a949c` and on the tutorial chronicle branch. The smoke is a compatibility check of the pre-disclosure v2 flow using an `edictLegacyAccess=true` account. There was more than one cause. Behaviour created by the staged disclosure work (`93d59959`) and later changes collided with stale smoke expectations in four places. All four are fixed and the smoke now passes end to end for the first time (final marker `HELLSCRIPT_TUTORIAL_RUNTIME_SMOKE_OK`). While fixing the fourth, a regression introduced by the first (app) fix was found and fixed as well. During the investigation the chronicle branch (PR #52), the passive tuning (PR #55) and the Hunt Edict native port (PR #53) were merged into `main` one after the other, so the final verification was done on a tree that includes all three merges.\n\n## 1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed\n\nBefore A2, `DrawSelectedGroup` excluded the Auto potion group (`survival.potion`) from quick pickers for every account. [Disclosure rules](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core/HuntEdictProgression.cs) already restricted the scope for new accounts, but legacy accounts needed the picker, which the historical fix restored. Current option editing belongs to the [side-menu sheet](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.EdictCatalog.cs), while recipe selection belongs to the [Presets & Share popup](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/EdictPresetsWindow.cs). The deleted window methods do not exist in these current files.\n\nThe v2 survival lesson (`GameUI.SurvivalLessonStep`) tells legacy accounts to press `edict-quick-picker-global/survival.potion`. The button did not exist, so `LessonTarget` returned null and the gate showed its line without a target. The gate releases input after 2 s, so the player is not trapped, but the line points at a button that does not exist and that way of finishing the lesson is unavailable. The smoke's `FollowGate` waits 120 s for a target and then fails.\n\nThe fix removes the group-name check so that `Quick` alone decides. For legacy accounts the `Auto potion` group shows the quick-preset picker first again, like the other groups (the behaviour before `93d59959`). One check was added to `HuntEdictProgressionTests` to pin the two cases of `Quick`.\n\nJudgement: either the picker could be restored or the v2 lesson could be changed. The app picker was restored because `Quick` allows every scope for legacy accounts, the documentation promises that existing accounts keep their access and that in-progress v2 saves finish on the old flow, and the coach tip `death-potion` recommends a preset of this scope. If the intent was that even legacy accounts see only the direct potion options, change the v2 lesson instead of keeping this fix.\n\nMerge conflict: PR #53 moved this condition into `HuntEdictWindow.QuickAllowed` and carried the potion-group exclusion along, which conflicted with PR #54. Its design document records the missing potion picker as the state of the code at the time, not as a decision about legacy accounts. At the merge the port's structure was kept and the two conditions of this fix (`Quick` decides; the v3 prologue has no picker) were moved inside `QuickAllowed`, so the new chip subtitle follows the same rule. The port's contract smoke uses staged accounts only, and its other smokes were adapted to pass with or without a picker, so they are not affected. Because the same exclusion came up independently on two branches, the decision to keep the potion picker for legacy accounts should be confirmed once more in review.\n\nRegression and follow-up fix: the fix as first pushed had a regression, found while writing the replay check. A replay always runs the v3 lesson, but its window still reads the real account. For a legacy account `Quick` is true, so the picker was also drawn in the v3 HP lesson window and hid `edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent`, the control the lesson points at ([screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/replay-r2-picker-hides-hp-option.png)). Before the fix the potion group had no picker, so that path worked. The same condition now also requires `!ProgressivePrologue`, so the v3 prologue shows direct options only, whatever the account (`ed79f12f`). New accounts and the v2 lesson are unchanged. This is a window condition that EditMode cannot test; the replay check is its test.\n\n## 2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed\n\nWith the picker visible the same run was blocked after the town arrival by the daily attendance window. When the greeting closes, `GameUI.TickAttendance` opens the attendance window as designed, and `ShowAttendance` cancels the town walk in progress with `Town.Cancel()`. The step waiting for the walk to the rift keeper timed out. The smoke now saves \"hide for today\" for both attendance popups and closes an open one, the way several other smokes do. Why the same smoke passed on 2026-09-30 without this was not investigated.\n\n## 3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed\n\nThe F07 step stalled next. `TryEdictNotice` (`93d59959`) shows one notice card in town whenever a result settles. After the F06 step the town went idle and the `Retry with modified settings` card opened and blocked the walk to the training ground. Steps F05 to F07 drive the same guides by hand, so `hintsHidden` is turned on once the first rift is over and the hero is back in town. It is set after the first rift so that the existing check that no automatic popup interrupts that rift keeps its meaning.\n\n## 4. The replay — smoke, fixed\n\nRuns 3 and 4 stopped in the final replay segment. `GameController.BeginTutorial(replay)` builds a fresh account with `GameStore.NewAccount`, so even a legacy account's replay always runs the v3 flow. The first v3 segment has a single dialogue, while the smoke waited for `tutorial-continue` twice as in v2. The second wait timed out after 15 s.\n\n`ReplayAcceptance` in `RuntimeTutorialSmoke.Progression.cs` now follows the replay through the v3 lesson. `FollowProgressiveGate` presses the comparison's observation areas (A/B), the final choice and the HP threshold number field with real pointers. It checks that the final choice and the HP threshold are saved on the replay's own hero, and that a replay played to the end leaves the real account's equipment, economy and progression unchanged. It copies the choreography of `ProgressiveAcceptance` without that smoke's first-run checks. The two were not merged into one loop, because that would mean re-verifying `ProgressiveAcceptance` (the v3 first-run check). A timeout in the new helper leaves the same screen and window-list evidence as `Until`.\n\nThe replay alone was run three times on a clone-only shortcut (not in the repository). The first run stalled in the HP lesson, with no target for 60 s. The second, with timeout diagnostics added, showed the regression of section 1. After the fix the third run passed in 1 min 43 s.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Run | Code | First launch | Second launch |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reported baseline | `ee5a949c`, chronicle branch | passes | fails after about 170 s: survival lesson, no target |\n| 1 | picker fix only | passes, 48.6 s | fails after 125.6 s: attendance window after arrival |\n| 2 | + attendance suppression | passes, 47.0 s | fails after 450.5 s: edict notice card at F07 |\n| 3 | + hints hidden after the first rift | passes, 55.3 s | fails after 381.2 s: replay |\n| 4 | run 3 changes + merged `main` (`17dc75e9`, chronicle PR #52) | passes, 47.9 s | fails after 462.7 s: replay (same point as run 3) |\n| 5 | run 4 + no picker in the v3 prologue + replay choreography | passes, 47.7 s | passes, 533.4 s |\n| 6 | run 5 + merged `main` (`a94bb636`, passive tuning PR #55) | passes, 45.6 s | passes, 492.2 s |\n| 7 | run 6 + merged `main` (`92407a06`, Hunt Edict native port PR #53) | passes, 46.7 s | passes, 437.2 s |\n\nThe second launch of run 5 passed the 10 pointer steps of the survival lesson (potion picker → `Extra survival supplies` → dodge group → picker → `Avoid all warnings` → save → close), the kill, reward and arrival dialogue, the regular first rift, F05, F06, F07 training and retry, the late-unlock briefing, the supported enhancement and the replay ([all PASS sentences](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt)). There is no error in the log. In runs 1 to 4 the per-step PASS sentences are written once at the end of the smoke, so a mid-run failure leaves none; progress there was judged from the evidence files written in order and from the failure point.\n\nThe second launches of runs 6 and 7 also produced the same 17 PASS sentences and have no error in the log ([all of them, run 6](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run6-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt)). Run 7 is the tree after the port rebuilt the window surface. The potion picker of the survival lesson, the v3 guidance of the replay, the edict notice card and the attendance handling all passed unchanged in the new window.\n\nThe five related EditMode classes (`HuntEdictProgressionTests` 37, `HuntEdictQuickPresetTests` 11, `TutorialProgressionTests` 33, `TutorialChapterTests` 6 and the port's `HuntEdictSentenceTests` 6) passed 93 of 93 on the final tree. The first four classes also passed 87 of 87 on the code of runs 5 and 6. The added test pins `Quick`'s values and does not reproduce the original symptom. That symptom was a window condition, so the smoke is the check.\n\nThe v3 first-run acceptance smoke (`-hellscriptEdictProgressionSmoke`) was run because the `!ProgressivePrologue` condition of section 1 touches the v3 prologue window of new accounts. Before the port merge, both the fixed code and an executable built from the same files of `main` before the fix passed the first launch. Their second launch failed after 95 to 97 s at the same point with the same evidence, `A committed progression change did not reveal its tab.` ([fixed code](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure.txt), [before](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-baseline.txt)). That was a stale `highestClear=3` expectation after the chronicle changed the edict ladder, and PR #53 fixed it. On the final merged tree the smoke gets past that point and its second launch times out in an `Until` on the plaza with the daily attendance window open ([screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-attendance-window-after-port.png), [record](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-after-port.txt)). That smoke does not hide the attendance popup, which looks like the same kind of problem as section 2, but which `Until` it was was not labelled or diagnosed. Either way the stretch this change touches (comparison lesson, HP lesson, boss, arrival, 10 town-edict layout profiles) passed, and the remaining failure is unrelated to this change and was not fixed.\n\nEvidence: [run log](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/runs.json), failure screens of runs 1 to 3 ([1](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run1-timeout-attendance-popup.png), [2](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run2-timeout-edict-notice.png), [3](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run3-timeout-replay-v3.png)), the [run 4 failure record](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run4-failure.txt), the regression screen, the survival lesson [picker step](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-04-potion-picker.png), [preset choice](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-05-careful-choice.png) and [save step](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-09-save.png), the [rift preparation screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/first-rift-preparation.png), the [replay completion screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-replay-complete.png) and the EditMode results [before the merges](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-premerge.xml) and [final](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-final.xml). Executable hashes and the build and run commands are in the run log. Build and smoke outputs stay in a temporary task path; only the evidence above is kept in the repository.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The pre-fix executable was not re-run in this tree. The cause was judged from the reported failure, code analysis and the pass at the same point after the fix. Only the v3 acceptance smoke was run on pre-fix code, for the comparison above.\n- The full EditMode suite and the other smokes were not run. The second launch of the v3 acceptance smoke does not complete because that smoke does not hide the attendance window. The shared-UI smoke (`-hellscriptSharedUiSmoke`), which walks every group's picker with a legacy account, was not run either. In the window the port rebuilt, the legacy potion picker was checked only through the v2 survival lesson.\n- The real screen of a new account after this change was not opened by hand. It was checked through the v3 acceptance smoke's HP lesson and through `Quick` returning the same values.\n- In the smoke fixture the picker reads `Current settings` while the lesson line says `Balanced supplies`. The fixture is a hybrid account (a fresh hero under a legacy flag). It looks like the new hero's automatic potion buying being off, which matches no preset, but that was not confirmed and it was not changed.\n- macOS synthetic pointer verification only; not a physical mobile device and not a user-comprehension test.\n", "html": "<blockquote><strong>2026-10-28 A2 correction:<\/strong> References to the large edict window, ≡ menu and their dedicated components or smokes are historical. Use the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs\">current entry points<\/a> and <a href=\"#/page/hunt-edict-window-removal-20261028.en\">replacement screens and source owners<\/a>. Earlier captures and test counts describe the earlier implementation.<\/blockquote><p>Updated: 2026-10-05 · <a href=\"#/page/tutorial-smoke-stall-20261005\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>The second launch of <code>-hellscriptTutorialSmoke<\/code> (<code>-hellscriptTutorialResume<\/code>) was reported to fail after about 170 s with <code>Timed out following the prologue gate: survival lesson target=<\/code>, on <code>origin/main<\/code> at <code>ee5a949c<\/code> and on the tutorial chronicle branch. The smoke is a compatibility check of the pre-disclosure v2 flow using an <code>edictLegacyAccess=true<\/code> account. There was more than one cause. Behaviour created by the staged disclosure work (<code>93d59959<\/code>) and later changes collided with stale smoke expectations in four places. All four are fixed and the smoke now passes end to end for the first time (final marker <code>HELLSCRIPT_TUTORIAL_RUNTIME_SMOKE_OK<\/code>). While fixing the fourth, a regression introduced by the first (app) fix was found and fixed as well. During the investigation the chronicle branch (PR #52), the passive tuning (PR #55) and the Hunt Edict native port (PR #53) were merged into <code>main<\/code> one after the other, so the final verification was done on a tree that includes all three merges.<\/p><h2 id=\"1-the-potion-picker-in-the-survival-lesson--app-fixed\">1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed<\/h2><p>Before A2, <code>DrawSelectedGroup<\/code> excluded the Auto potion group (<code>survival.potion<\/code>) from quick pickers for every account. <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core/HuntEdictProgression.cs\">Disclosure rules<\/a> already restricted the scope for new accounts, but legacy accounts needed the picker, which the historical fix restored. Current option editing belongs to the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.EdictCatalog.cs\">side-menu sheet<\/a>, while recipe selection belongs to the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/EdictPresetsWindow.cs\">Presets &amp; Share popup<\/a>. The deleted window methods do not exist in these current files.<\/p><p>The v2 survival lesson (<code>GameUI.SurvivalLessonStep<\/code>) tells legacy accounts to press <code>edict-quick-picker-global/survival.potion<\/code>. The button did not exist, so <code>LessonTarget<\/code> returned null and the gate showed its line without a target. The gate releases input after 2 s, so the player is not trapped, but the line points at a button that does not exist and that way of finishing the lesson is unavailable. The smoke&#x27;s <code>FollowGate<\/code> waits 120 s for a target and then fails.<\/p><p>The fix removes the group-name check so that <code>Quick<\/code> alone decides. For legacy accounts the <code>Auto potion<\/code> group shows the quick-preset picker first again, like the other groups (the behaviour before <code>93d59959<\/code>). One check was added to <code>HuntEdictProgressionTests<\/code> to pin the two cases of <code>Quick<\/code>.<\/p><p>Judgement: either the picker could be restored or the v2 lesson could be changed. The app picker was restored because <code>Quick<\/code> allows every scope for legacy accounts, the documentation promises that existing accounts keep their access and that in-progress v2 saves finish on the old flow, and the coach tip <code>death-potion<\/code> recommends a preset of this scope. If the intent was that even legacy accounts see only the direct potion options, change the v2 lesson instead of keeping this fix.<\/p><p>Merge conflict: PR #53 moved this condition into <code>HuntEdictWindow.QuickAllowed<\/code> and carried the potion-group exclusion along, which conflicted with PR #54. Its design document records the missing potion picker as the state of the code at the time, not as a decision about legacy accounts. At the merge the port&#x27;s structure was kept and the two conditions of this fix (<code>Quick<\/code> decides; the v3 prologue has no picker) were moved inside <code>QuickAllowed<\/code>, so the new chip subtitle follows the same rule. The port&#x27;s contract smoke uses staged accounts only, and its other smokes were adapted to pass with or without a picker, so they are not affected. Because the same exclusion came up independently on two branches, the decision to keep the potion picker for legacy accounts should be confirmed once more in review.<\/p><p>Regression and follow-up fix: the fix as first pushed had a regression, found while writing the replay check. A replay always runs the v3 lesson, but its window still reads the real account. For a legacy account <code>Quick<\/code> is true, so the picker was also drawn in the v3 HP lesson window and hid <code>edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent<\/code>, the control the lesson points at (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/replay-r2-picker-hides-hp-option.png\">screen<\/a>). Before the fix the potion group had no picker, so that path worked. The same condition now also requires <code>!ProgressivePrologue<\/code>, so the v3 prologue shows direct options only, whatever the account (<code>ed79f12f<\/code>). New accounts and the v2 lesson are unchanged. This is a window condition that EditMode cannot test; the replay check is its test.<\/p><h2 id=\"2-the-attendance-popup--smoke-fixed\">2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>With the picker visible the same run was blocked after the town arrival by the daily attendance window. When the greeting closes, <code>GameUI.TickAttendance<\/code> opens the attendance window as designed, and <code>ShowAttendance<\/code> cancels the town walk in progress with <code>Town.Cancel()<\/code>. The step waiting for the walk to the rift keeper timed out. The smoke now saves &quot;hide for today&quot; for both attendance popups and closes an open one, the way several other smokes do. Why the same smoke passed on 2026-09-30 without this was not investigated.<\/p><h2 id=\"3-the-edict-notice-card--smoke-fixed\">3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>The F07 step stalled next. <code>TryEdictNotice<\/code> (<code>93d59959<\/code>) shows one notice card in town whenever a result settles. After the F06 step the town went idle and the <code>Retry with modified settings<\/code> card opened and blocked the walk to the training ground. Steps F05 to F07 drive the same guides by hand, so <code>hintsHidden<\/code> is turned on once the first rift is over and the hero is back in town. It is set after the first rift so that the existing check that no automatic popup interrupts that rift keeps its meaning.<\/p><h2 id=\"4-the-replay--smoke-fixed\">4. The replay — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>Runs 3 and 4 stopped in the final replay segment. <code>GameController.BeginTutorial(replay)<\/code> builds a fresh account with <code>GameStore.NewAccount<\/code>, so even a legacy account&#x27;s replay always runs the v3 flow. The first v3 segment has a single dialogue, while the smoke waited for <code>tutorial-continue<\/code> twice as in v2. The second wait timed out after 15 s.<\/p><p><code>ReplayAcceptance<\/code> in <code>RuntimeTutorialSmoke.Progression.cs<\/code> now follows the replay through the v3 lesson. <code>FollowProgressiveGate<\/code> presses the comparison&#x27;s observation areas (A/B), the final choice and the HP threshold number field with real pointers. It checks that the final choice and the HP threshold are saved on the replay&#x27;s own hero, and that a replay played to the end leaves the real account&#x27;s equipment, economy and progression unchanged. It copies the choreography of <code>ProgressiveAcceptance<\/code> without that smoke&#x27;s first-run checks. The two were not merged into one loop, because that would mean re-verifying <code>ProgressiveAcceptance<\/code> (the v3 first-run check). A timeout in the new helper leaves the same screen and window-list evidence as <code>Until<\/code>.<\/p><p>The replay alone was run three times on a clone-only shortcut (not in the repository). The first run stalled in the HP lesson, with no target for 60 s. The second, with timeout diagnostics added, showed the regression of section 1. After the fix the third run passed in 1 min 43 s.<\/p><h2 id=\"verification\">Verification<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Run<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Code<\/th><th scope=\"col\">First launch<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Second launch<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Reported baseline<\/td><td><code>ee5a949c<\/code>, chronicle branch<\/td><td>passes<\/td><td>fails after about 170 s: survival lesson, no target<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>picker fix only<\/td><td>passes, 48.6 s<\/td><td>fails after 125.6 s: attendance window after arrival<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>+ attendance suppression<\/td><td>passes, 47.0 s<\/td><td>fails after 450.5 s: edict notice card at F07<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>+ hints hidden after the first rift<\/td><td>passes, 55.3 s<\/td><td>fails after 381.2 s: replay<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>run 3 changes + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>17dc75e9<\/code>, chronicle PR #52)<\/td><td>passes, 47.9 s<\/td><td>fails after 462.7 s: replay (same point as run 3)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>run 4 + no picker in the v3 prologue + replay choreography<\/td><td>passes, 47.7 s<\/td><td>passes, 533.4 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>run 5 + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>a94bb636<\/code>, passive tuning PR #55)<\/td><td>passes, 45.6 s<\/td><td>passes, 492.2 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td>run 6 + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>92407a06<\/code>, Hunt Edict native port PR #53)<\/td><td>passes, 46.7 s<\/td><td>passes, 437.2 s<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The second launch of run 5 passed the 10 pointer steps of the survival lesson (potion picker → <code>Extra survival supplies<\/code> → dodge group → picker → <code>Avoid all warnings<\/code> → save → close), the kill, reward and arrival dialogue, the regular first rift, F05, F06, F07 training and retry, the late-unlock briefing, the supported enhancement and the replay (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt\">all PASS sentences<\/a>). There is no error in the log. In runs 1 to 4 the per-step PASS sentences are written once at the end of the smoke, so a mid-run failure leaves none; progress there was judged from the evidence files written in order and from the failure point.<\/p><p>The second launches of runs 6 and 7 also produced the same 17 PASS sentences and have no error in the log (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run6-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt\">all of them, run 6<\/a>). Run 7 is the tree after the port rebuilt the window surface. The potion picker of the survival lesson, the v3 guidance of the replay, the edict notice card and the attendance handling all passed unchanged in the new window.<\/p><p>The five related EditMode classes (<code>HuntEdictProgressionTests<\/code> 37, <code>HuntEdictQuickPresetTests<\/code> 11, <code>TutorialProgressionTests<\/code> 33, <code>TutorialChapterTests<\/code> 6 and the port&#x27;s <code>HuntEdictSentenceTests<\/code> 6) passed 93 of 93 on the final tree. The first four classes also passed 87 of 87 on the code of runs 5 and 6. The added test pins <code>Quick<\/code>&#x27;s values and does not reproduce the original symptom. That symptom was a window condition, so the smoke is the check.<\/p><p>The v3 first-run acceptance smoke (<code>-hellscriptEdictProgressionSmoke<\/code>) was run because the <code>!ProgressivePrologue<\/code> condition of section 1 touches the v3 prologue window of new accounts. Before the port merge, both the fixed code and an executable built from the same files of <code>main<\/code> before the fix passed the first launch. Their second launch failed after 95 to 97 s at the same point with the same evidence, <code>A committed progression change did not reveal its tab.<\/code> (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure.txt\">fixed code<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-baseline.txt\">before<\/a>). That was a stale <code>highestClear=3<\/code> expectation after the chronicle changed the edict ladder, and PR #53 fixed it. On the final merged tree the smoke gets past that point and its second launch times out in an <code>Until<\/code> on the plaza with the daily attendance window open (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-attendance-window-after-port.png\">screen<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-after-port.txt\">record<\/a>). That smoke does not hide the attendance popup, which looks like the same kind of problem as section 2, but which <code>Until<\/code> it was was not labelled or diagnosed. Either way the stretch this change touches (comparison lesson, HP lesson, boss, arrival, 10 town-edict layout profiles) passed, and the remaining failure is unrelated to this change and was not fixed.<\/p><p>Evidence: <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/runs.json\">run log<\/a>, failure screens of runs 1 to 3 (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run1-timeout-attendance-popup.png\">1<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run2-timeout-edict-notice.png\">2<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run3-timeout-replay-v3.png\">3<\/a>), the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run4-failure.txt\">run 4 failure record<\/a>, the regression screen, the survival lesson <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-04-potion-picker.png\">picker step<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-05-careful-choice.png\">preset choice<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-09-save.png\">save step<\/a>, the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/first-rift-preparation.png\">rift preparation screen<\/a>, the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-replay-complete.png\">replay completion screen<\/a> and the EditMode results <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-premerge.xml\">before the merges<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-final.xml\">final<\/a>. Executable hashes and the build and run commands are in the run log. Build and smoke outputs stay in a temporary task path; only the evidence above is kept in the repository.<\/p><h2 id=\"not-verified\">Not verified<\/h2><ul><li>The pre-fix executable was not re-run in this tree. The cause was judged from the reported failure, code analysis and the pass at the same point after the fix. Only the v3 acceptance smoke was run on pre-fix code, for the comparison above.<\/li><li>The full EditMode suite and the other smokes were not run. The second launch of the v3 acceptance smoke does not complete because that smoke does not hide the attendance window. The shared-UI smoke (<code>-hellscriptSharedUiSmoke<\/code>), which walks every group&#x27;s picker with a legacy account, was not run either. In the window the port rebuilt, the legacy potion picker was checked only through the v2 survival lesson.<\/li><li>The real screen of a new account after this change was not opened by hand. It was checked through the v3 acceptance smoke&#x27;s HP lesson and through <code>Quick<\/code> returning the same values.<\/li><li>In the smoke fixture the picker reads <code>Current settings<\/code> while the lesson line says <code>Balanced supplies<\/code>. The fixture is a hybrid account (a fresh hero under a legacy flag). It looks like the new hero&#x27;s automatic potion buying being off, which matches no preset, but that was not confirmed and it was not changed.<\/li><li>macOS synthetic pointer verification only; not a physical mobile device and not a user-comprehension test.<\/li><\/ul>", "headings": [{"id": "1-the-potion-picker-in-the-survival-lesson--app-fixed", "title": "1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed"}, {"id": "2-the-attendance-popup--smoke-fixed", "title": "2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "3-the-edict-notice-card--smoke-fixed", "title": "3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "4-the-replay--smoke-fixed", "title": "4. The replay — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "verification", "title": "Verification"}, {"id": "not-verified", "title": "Not verified"}]}, {"body": "# Tutorial compatibility smoke stall investigation\n\n> **2026-10-28 A2 correction:** References to the large edict window, ≡ menu and their dedicated components or smokes are historical. Use the [current entry points](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs) and [replacement screens and source owners](Hunt_Edict_Window_Removal_20261028.en.md). Earlier captures and test counts describe the earlier implementation.\n\nUpdated: 2026-10-05 · [한국어](Tutorial_Smoke_Stall_20261005.md)\n\nThe second launch of `-hellscriptTutorialSmoke` (`-hellscriptTutorialResume`) was reported to fail after about 170 s with `Timed out following the prologue gate: survival lesson target=`, on `origin/main` at `ee5a949c` and on the tutorial chronicle branch. The smoke is a compatibility check of the pre-disclosure v2 flow using an `edictLegacyAccess=true` account. There was more than one cause. Behaviour created by the staged disclosure work (`93d59959`) and later changes collided with stale smoke expectations in four places. All four are fixed and the smoke now passes end to end for the first time (final marker `HELLSCRIPT_TUTORIAL_RUNTIME_SMOKE_OK`). While fixing the fourth, a regression introduced by the first (app) fix was found and fixed as well. During the investigation the chronicle branch (PR #52), the passive tuning (PR #55), the Hunt Edict native port (PR #53) and the tutorial wiring (PR #56) were merged into `main` one after the other, so the final verification was done on a tree that includes all four merges. After the last merge one more intermittent failure showed up, a missed pointer in the F05 step, and the smoke's `Tap` was fixed (section 5).\n\n## 1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed\n\nBefore A2, `DrawSelectedGroup` excluded the Auto potion group (`survival.potion`) from quick pickers for every account. [Disclosure rules](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core/HuntEdictProgression.cs) already restricted the scope for new accounts, but legacy accounts needed the picker, which the historical fix restored. Current option editing belongs to the [side-menu sheet](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.EdictCatalog.cs), while recipe selection belongs to the [Presets & Share popup](../../Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/EdictPresetsWindow.cs). The deleted window methods do not exist in these current files.\n\nThe v2 survival lesson (`GameUI.SurvivalLessonStep`) tells legacy accounts to press `edict-quick-picker-global/survival.potion`. The button did not exist, so `LessonTarget` returned null and the gate showed its line without a target. The gate releases input after 2 s, so the player is not trapped, but the line points at a button that does not exist and that way of finishing the lesson is unavailable. The smoke's `FollowGate` waits 120 s for a target and then fails.\n\nThe fix removes the group-name check so that `Quick` alone decides. For legacy accounts the `Auto potion` group shows the quick-preset picker first again, like the other groups (the behaviour before `93d59959`). One check was added to `HuntEdictProgressionTests` to pin the two cases of `Quick`.\n\nJudgement: either the picker could be restored or the v2 lesson could be changed. The app picker was restored because `Quick` allows every scope for legacy accounts, the documentation promises that existing accounts keep their access and that in-progress v2 saves finish on the old flow, and the coach tip `death-potion` recommends a preset of this scope. If the intent was that even legacy accounts see only the direct potion options, change the v2 lesson instead of keeping this fix.\n\nMerge conflict: PR #53 moved this condition into `HuntEdictWindow.QuickAllowed` and carried the potion-group exclusion along, which conflicted with PR #54. Its design document records the missing potion picker as the state of the code at the time, not as a decision about legacy accounts. At the merge the port's structure was kept and the two conditions of this fix (`Quick` decides; the v3 prologue has no picker) were moved inside `QuickAllowed`, so the new chip subtitle follows the same rule. The port's contract smoke uses staged accounts only, and its other smokes were adapted to pass with or without a picker, so they are not affected. Because the same exclusion came up independently on two branches, the decision to keep the potion picker for legacy accounts should be confirmed once more in review.\n\nRegression and follow-up fix: the fix as first pushed had a regression, found while writing the replay check. A replay always runs the v3 lesson, but its window still reads the real account. For a legacy account `Quick` is true, so the picker was also drawn in the v3 HP lesson window and hid `edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent`, the control the lesson points at ([screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/replay-r2-picker-hides-hp-option.png)). Before the fix the potion group had no picker, so that path worked. The same condition now also requires `!ProgressivePrologue`, so the v3 prologue shows direct options only, whatever the account (`ed79f12f`). New accounts and the v2 lesson are unchanged. This is a window condition that EditMode cannot test; the replay check is its test.\n\n## 2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed\n\nWith the picker visible the same run was blocked after the town arrival by the daily attendance window. When the greeting closes, `GameUI.TickAttendance` opens the attendance window as designed, and `ShowAttendance` cancels the town walk in progress with `Town.Cancel()`. The step waiting for the walk to the rift keeper timed out. The smoke now saves \"hide for today\" for both attendance popups and closes an open one, the way several other smokes do. Why the same smoke passed on 2026-09-30 without this was not investigated.\n\n## 3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed\n\nThe F07 step stalled next. `TryEdictNotice` (`93d59959`) shows one notice card in town whenever a result settles. After the F06 step the town went idle and the `Retry with modified settings` card opened and blocked the walk to the training ground. Steps F05 to F07 drive the same guides by hand, so `hintsHidden` is turned on once the first rift is over and the hero is back in town. It is set after the first rift so that the existing check that no automatic popup interrupts that rift keeps its meaning.\n\n## 4. The replay — smoke, fixed\n\nRuns 3 and 4 stopped in the final replay segment. `GameController.BeginTutorial(replay)` builds a fresh account with `GameStore.NewAccount`, so even a legacy account's replay always runs the v3 flow. The first v3 segment has a single dialogue, while the smoke waited for `tutorial-continue` twice as in v2. The second wait timed out after 15 s.\n\n`ReplayAcceptance` in `RuntimeTutorialSmoke.Progression.cs` now follows the replay through the v3 lesson. `FollowProgressiveGate` presses the comparison's observation areas (A/B), the final choice and the HP threshold number field with real pointers. It checks that the final choice and the HP threshold are saved on the replay's own hero, and that a replay played to the end leaves the real account's equipment, economy and progression unchanged. It copies the choreography of `ProgressiveAcceptance` without that smoke's first-run checks. The two were not merged into one loop, because that would mean re-verifying `ProgressiveAcceptance` (the v3 first-run check). A timeout in the new helper leaves the same screen and window-list evidence as `Until`.\n\nThe replay alone was run three times on a clone-only shortcut (not in the repository). The first run stalled in the HP lesson, with no target for 60 s. The second, with timeout diagnostics added, showed the regression of section 1. After the fix the third run passed in 1 min 43 s.\n\n## 5. Window rebuild and the pointer — smoke, fixed\n\nOn the tree with PR #56 merged, the second launch sometimes stopped in the F05 step with `Pointer blocked: edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent` (run 9). The pointer had landed on the window frame and the backdrop only. Runs 8 and 10 passed the same step on the same code, so it is intermittent. The cause is inferred from the code, because the failing run left no screenshot. The guide poll (every 0.25 s) puts a caption band into the window the first time it finds a guide's control, and the window is rebuilt, which replaces its controls (`RefreshTutorialAnchor`, `SyncGuideCaption`). The smoke's `Tap` re-fetches a control after scrolling, but a pointer fired just after the rebuild can land before the new layout has settled.\n\nThe fix: when the pointer misses, `Tap` re-fetches the control every frame and waits up to 0.6 s for the pointer to land. If something keeps covering the control it still fails as before, and then leaves a screenshot and the hit list (`pointer-blocked.png`, `pointer-blocked.txt`). After the fix the same tree passed the full smoke three times in a row (runs 11 to 13). Before it, one of three attempts on that tree stopped at this step. The sample is small, so the intermittent failure is not claimed to be gone.\n\nMidnight: the attendance hide lasts only until midnight (KST). A run that crosses 00:00 reopens the attendance window and stalls at the next town step. Run 8 started at 23:53 and failed that way ([screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run8-timeout-attendance-after-midnight.png), attendance day 2 of 7), and the same executable passed this step after midnight. This was judged from the screen, the clock and the code and was not reproduced separately. Do not start the smoke just before midnight.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Run | Code | First launch | Second launch |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Reported baseline | `ee5a949c`, chronicle branch | passes | fails after about 170 s: survival lesson, no target |\n| 1 | picker fix only | passes, 48.6 s | fails after 125.6 s: attendance window after arrival |\n| 2 | + attendance suppression | passes, 47.0 s | fails after 450.5 s: edict notice card at F07 |\n| 3 | + hints hidden after the first rift | passes, 55.3 s | fails after 381.2 s: replay |\n| 4 | run 3 changes + merged `main` (`17dc75e9`, chronicle PR #52) | passes, 47.9 s | fails after 462.7 s: replay (same point as run 3) |\n| 5 | run 4 + no picker in the v3 prologue + replay choreography | passes, 47.7 s | passes, 533.4 s |\n| 6 | run 5 + merged `main` (`a94bb636`, passive tuning PR #55) | passes, 45.6 s | passes, 492.2 s |\n| 7 | run 6 + merged `main` (`92407a06`, Hunt Edict native port PR #53) | passes, 46.7 s | passes, 437.2 s |\n| 8 | run 7 + merged `main` (`b1970567`, tutorial wiring PR #56) | passes, 45.6 s | fails after 367.8 s: the run crossed midnight and the attendance window reopened (F07 step) |\n| 9 | same executable as run 8, after midnight | passes, 41.8 s | fails after 402.8 s: pointer missed in the F05 step |\n| 10 | run 9 + missed-pointer diagnostics (no behaviour change) | passes, 45.0 s | passes, 507.1 s |\n| 11 | run 10 + `Tap` settling | passes, 44.8 s | passes, 446.8 s |\n| 12 | same executable | passes, 41.4 s | passes, 539.1 s |\n| 13 | same executable | passes, 41.2 s | passes, 538.5 s |\n\nThe second launch of run 5 passed the 10 pointer steps of the survival lesson (potion picker → `Extra survival supplies` → dodge group → picker → `Avoid all warnings` → save → close), the kill, reward and arrival dialogue, the regular first rift, F05, F06, F07 training and retry, the late-unlock briefing, the supported enhancement and the replay ([all PASS sentences](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt)). There is no error in the log. In runs 1 to 4 the per-step PASS sentences are written once at the end of the smoke, so a mid-run failure leaves none; progress there was judged from the evidence files written in order and from the failure point.\n\nThe second launches of runs 6 and 7 also produced the same 17 PASS sentences and have no error in the log ([all of them, run 6](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run6-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt)). The passing runs 10 to 13 produced the same 17 ([all of them, run 13](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run13-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt)); only the hero level in the F06 sentence (3 or 4, from the natural leveling of the first rift) varies. Run 7 is the tree after the port rebuilt the window surface. The potion picker of the survival lesson, the v3 guidance of the replay, the edict notice card and the attendance handling all passed unchanged in the new window.\n\nThe seven related EditMode classes (`HuntEdictProgressionTests` 37, `HuntEdictQuickPresetTests` 11, `TutorialProgressionTests` 33, `TutorialChapterTests` 6, the port's `HuntEdictSentenceTests` 6, and the tutorial wiring's `EdictGuidanceTests` 9 and `PrologueGateTests` 8) passed 110 of 110 on the final tree. The first four classes also passed 87 of 87 on the code of runs 5 and 6. The added test pins `Quick`'s values and does not reproduce the original symptom. That symptom was a window condition, so the smoke is the check.\n\nThe v3 first-run acceptance smoke (`-hellscriptEdictProgressionSmoke`) was run because the `!ProgressivePrologue` condition of section 1 touches the v3 prologue window of new accounts. Before the port merge, both the fixed code and an executable built from the same files of `main` before the fix passed the first launch. Their second launch failed after 95 to 97 s at the same point with the same evidence, `A committed progression change did not reveal its tab.` ([fixed code](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure.txt), [before](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-baseline.txt)). That was a stale `highestClear=3` expectation after the chronicle changed the edict ladder, and PR #53 fixed it. Right after the port merge the smoke got past that point and its second launch timed out in an `Until` on the plaza with the daily attendance window open ([screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-attendance-window-after-port.png), [record](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-after-port.txt)). PR #56 added the attendance hide to that smoke too, so on the final tree with the tutorial wiring merged it passes through the second launch (103.2 s, [all PASS sentences](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-result.txt)). That run includes the stretch this change touches: comparison lesson, HP lesson, boss and arrival. None of these stops was caused by this change.\n\nEvidence: [run log](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/runs.json), failure screens of runs 1 to 3 ([1](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run1-timeout-attendance-popup.png), [2](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run2-timeout-edict-notice.png), [3](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run3-timeout-replay-v3.png)), the [run 4 failure record](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run4-failure.txt), the regression screen, the survival lesson [picker step](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-04-potion-picker.png), [preset choice](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-05-careful-choice.png) and [save step](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-09-save.png), the [rift preparation screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/first-rift-preparation.png), the [replay completion screen](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-replay-complete.png) and the EditMode results [before the merges](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-premerge.xml) and [final](TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-final.xml). Executable hashes and the build and run commands are in the run log. Build and smoke outputs stay in a temporary task path; only the evidence above is kept in the repository.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The pre-fix executable was not re-run in this tree. The cause was judged from the reported failure, code analysis and the pass at the same point after the fix. Only the v3 acceptance smoke was run on pre-fix code, for the comparison above.\n- The full EditMode suite and the other smokes were not run. The shared-UI smoke (`-hellscriptSharedUiSmoke`), which walks every group's picker with a legacy account, was not run either. In the window the port rebuilt, the legacy potion picker was checked only through the v2 survival lesson.\n- The cause of the `Tap` settling fix is inferred from the code and there is no screenshot of the failing moment. The evidence is a small sample (one failure in three attempts before, three passes in a row after), so the intermittent failure is not claimed to be gone.\n- The real screen of a new account after this change was not opened by hand. It was checked through the v3 acceptance smoke's HP lesson and through `Quick` returning the same values.\n- In the smoke fixture the picker reads `Current settings` while the lesson line says `Balanced supplies`. The fixture is a hybrid account (a fresh hero under a legacy flag). It looks like the new hero's automatic potion buying being off, which matches no preset, but that was not confirmed and it was not changed.\n- macOS synthetic pointer verification only; not a physical mobile device and not a user-comprehension test.\n", "html": "<blockquote><strong>2026-10-28 A2 correction:<\/strong> References to the large edict window, ≡ menu and their dedicated components or smokes are historical. Use the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs\">current entry points<\/a> and <a href=\"#/page/hunt-edict-window-removal-20261028.en\">replacement screens and source owners<\/a>. Earlier captures and test counts describe the earlier implementation.<\/blockquote><p>Updated: 2026-10-05 · <a href=\"#/page/tutorial-smoke-stall-20261005\">한국어<\/a><\/p><p>The second launch of <code>-hellscriptTutorialSmoke<\/code> (<code>-hellscriptTutorialResume<\/code>) was reported to fail after about 170 s with <code>Timed out following the prologue gate: survival lesson target=<\/code>, on <code>origin/main<\/code> at <code>ee5a949c<\/code> and on the tutorial chronicle branch. The smoke is a compatibility check of the pre-disclosure v2 flow using an <code>edictLegacyAccess=true<\/code> account. There was more than one cause. Behaviour created by the staged disclosure work (<code>93d59959<\/code>) and later changes collided with stale smoke expectations in four places. All four are fixed and the smoke now passes end to end for the first time (final marker <code>HELLSCRIPT_TUTORIAL_RUNTIME_SMOKE_OK<\/code>). While fixing the fourth, a regression introduced by the first (app) fix was found and fixed as well. During the investigation the chronicle branch (PR #52), the passive tuning (PR #55), the Hunt Edict native port (PR #53) and the tutorial wiring (PR #56) were merged into <code>main<\/code> one after the other, so the final verification was done on a tree that includes all four merges. After the last merge one more intermittent failure showed up, a missed pointer in the F05 step, and the smoke&#x27;s <code>Tap<\/code> was fixed (section 5).<\/p><h2 id=\"1-the-potion-picker-in-the-survival-lesson--app-fixed\">1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed<\/h2><p>Before A2, <code>DrawSelectedGroup<\/code> excluded the Auto potion group (<code>survival.potion<\/code>) from quick pickers for every account. <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core/HuntEdictProgression.cs\">Disclosure rules<\/a> already restricted the scope for new accounts, but legacy accounts needed the picker, which the historical fix restored. Current option editing belongs to the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/GameUI.EdictCatalog.cs\">side-menu sheet<\/a>, while recipe selection belongs to the <a href=\"sources/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation/EdictPresetsWindow.cs\">Presets &amp; Share popup<\/a>. The deleted window methods do not exist in these current files.<\/p><p>The v2 survival lesson (<code>GameUI.SurvivalLessonStep<\/code>) tells legacy accounts to press <code>edict-quick-picker-global/survival.potion<\/code>. The button did not exist, so <code>LessonTarget<\/code> returned null and the gate showed its line without a target. The gate releases input after 2 s, so the player is not trapped, but the line points at a button that does not exist and that way of finishing the lesson is unavailable. The smoke&#x27;s <code>FollowGate<\/code> waits 120 s for a target and then fails.<\/p><p>The fix removes the group-name check so that <code>Quick<\/code> alone decides. For legacy accounts the <code>Auto potion<\/code> group shows the quick-preset picker first again, like the other groups (the behaviour before <code>93d59959<\/code>). One check was added to <code>HuntEdictProgressionTests<\/code> to pin the two cases of <code>Quick<\/code>.<\/p><p>Judgement: either the picker could be restored or the v2 lesson could be changed. The app picker was restored because <code>Quick<\/code> allows every scope for legacy accounts, the documentation promises that existing accounts keep their access and that in-progress v2 saves finish on the old flow, and the coach tip <code>death-potion<\/code> recommends a preset of this scope. If the intent was that even legacy accounts see only the direct potion options, change the v2 lesson instead of keeping this fix.<\/p><p>Merge conflict: PR #53 moved this condition into <code>HuntEdictWindow.QuickAllowed<\/code> and carried the potion-group exclusion along, which conflicted with PR #54. Its design document records the missing potion picker as the state of the code at the time, not as a decision about legacy accounts. At the merge the port&#x27;s structure was kept and the two conditions of this fix (<code>Quick<\/code> decides; the v3 prologue has no picker) were moved inside <code>QuickAllowed<\/code>, so the new chip subtitle follows the same rule. The port&#x27;s contract smoke uses staged accounts only, and its other smokes were adapted to pass with or without a picker, so they are not affected. Because the same exclusion came up independently on two branches, the decision to keep the potion picker for legacy accounts should be confirmed once more in review.<\/p><p>Regression and follow-up fix: the fix as first pushed had a regression, found while writing the replay check. A replay always runs the v3 lesson, but its window still reads the real account. For a legacy account <code>Quick<\/code> is true, so the picker was also drawn in the v3 HP lesson window and hid <code>edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent<\/code>, the control the lesson points at (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/replay-r2-picker-hides-hp-option.png\">screen<\/a>). Before the fix the potion group had no picker, so that path worked. The same condition now also requires <code>!ProgressivePrologue<\/code>, so the v3 prologue shows direct options only, whatever the account (<code>ed79f12f<\/code>). New accounts and the v2 lesson are unchanged. This is a window condition that EditMode cannot test; the replay check is its test.<\/p><h2 id=\"2-the-attendance-popup--smoke-fixed\">2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>With the picker visible the same run was blocked after the town arrival by the daily attendance window. When the greeting closes, <code>GameUI.TickAttendance<\/code> opens the attendance window as designed, and <code>ShowAttendance<\/code> cancels the town walk in progress with <code>Town.Cancel()<\/code>. The step waiting for the walk to the rift keeper timed out. The smoke now saves &quot;hide for today&quot; for both attendance popups and closes an open one, the way several other smokes do. Why the same smoke passed on 2026-09-30 without this was not investigated.<\/p><h2 id=\"3-the-edict-notice-card--smoke-fixed\">3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>The F07 step stalled next. <code>TryEdictNotice<\/code> (<code>93d59959<\/code>) shows one notice card in town whenever a result settles. After the F06 step the town went idle and the <code>Retry with modified settings<\/code> card opened and blocked the walk to the training ground. Steps F05 to F07 drive the same guides by hand, so <code>hintsHidden<\/code> is turned on once the first rift is over and the hero is back in town. It is set after the first rift so that the existing check that no automatic popup interrupts that rift keeps its meaning.<\/p><h2 id=\"4-the-replay--smoke-fixed\">4. The replay — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>Runs 3 and 4 stopped in the final replay segment. <code>GameController.BeginTutorial(replay)<\/code> builds a fresh account with <code>GameStore.NewAccount<\/code>, so even a legacy account&#x27;s replay always runs the v3 flow. The first v3 segment has a single dialogue, while the smoke waited for <code>tutorial-continue<\/code> twice as in v2. The second wait timed out after 15 s.<\/p><p><code>ReplayAcceptance<\/code> in <code>RuntimeTutorialSmoke.Progression.cs<\/code> now follows the replay through the v3 lesson. <code>FollowProgressiveGate<\/code> presses the comparison&#x27;s observation areas (A/B), the final choice and the HP threshold number field with real pointers. It checks that the final choice and the HP threshold are saved on the replay&#x27;s own hero, and that a replay played to the end leaves the real account&#x27;s equipment, economy and progression unchanged. It copies the choreography of <code>ProgressiveAcceptance<\/code> without that smoke&#x27;s first-run checks. The two were not merged into one loop, because that would mean re-verifying <code>ProgressiveAcceptance<\/code> (the v3 first-run check). A timeout in the new helper leaves the same screen and window-list evidence as <code>Until<\/code>.<\/p><p>The replay alone was run three times on a clone-only shortcut (not in the repository). The first run stalled in the HP lesson, with no target for 60 s. The second, with timeout diagnostics added, showed the regression of section 1. After the fix the third run passed in 1 min 43 s.<\/p><h2 id=\"5-window-rebuild-and-the-pointer--smoke-fixed\">5. Window rebuild and the pointer — smoke, fixed<\/h2><p>On the tree with PR #56 merged, the second launch sometimes stopped in the F05 step with <code>Pointer blocked: edict-option-survival.potionHpPercent<\/code> (run 9). The pointer had landed on the window frame and the backdrop only. Runs 8 and 10 passed the same step on the same code, so it is intermittent. The cause is inferred from the code, because the failing run left no screenshot. The guide poll (every 0.25 s) puts a caption band into the window the first time it finds a guide&#x27;s control, and the window is rebuilt, which replaces its controls (<code>RefreshTutorialAnchor<\/code>, <code>SyncGuideCaption<\/code>). The smoke&#x27;s <code>Tap<\/code> re-fetches a control after scrolling, but a pointer fired just after the rebuild can land before the new layout has settled.<\/p><p>The fix: when the pointer misses, <code>Tap<\/code> re-fetches the control every frame and waits up to 0.6 s for the pointer to land. If something keeps covering the control it still fails as before, and then leaves a screenshot and the hit list (<code>pointer-blocked.png<\/code>, <code>pointer-blocked.txt<\/code>). After the fix the same tree passed the full smoke three times in a row (runs 11 to 13). Before it, one of three attempts on that tree stopped at this step. The sample is small, so the intermittent failure is not claimed to be gone.<\/p><p>Midnight: the attendance hide lasts only until midnight (KST). A run that crosses 00:00 reopens the attendance window and stalls at the next town step. Run 8 started at 23:53 and failed that way (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run8-timeout-attendance-after-midnight.png\">screen<\/a>, attendance day 2 of 7), and the same executable passed this step after midnight. This was judged from the screen, the clock and the code and was not reproduced separately. Do not start the smoke just before midnight.<\/p><h2 id=\"verification\">Verification<\/h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Run<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Code<\/th><th scope=\"col\">First launch<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Second launch<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Reported baseline<\/td><td><code>ee5a949c<\/code>, chronicle branch<\/td><td>passes<\/td><td>fails after about 170 s: survival lesson, no target<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1<\/td><td>picker fix only<\/td><td>passes, 48.6 s<\/td><td>fails after 125.6 s: attendance window after arrival<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2<\/td><td>+ attendance suppression<\/td><td>passes, 47.0 s<\/td><td>fails after 450.5 s: edict notice card at F07<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3<\/td><td>+ hints hidden after the first rift<\/td><td>passes, 55.3 s<\/td><td>fails after 381.2 s: replay<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4<\/td><td>run 3 changes + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>17dc75e9<\/code>, chronicle PR #52)<\/td><td>passes, 47.9 s<\/td><td>fails after 462.7 s: replay (same point as run 3)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5<\/td><td>run 4 + no picker in the v3 prologue + replay choreography<\/td><td>passes, 47.7 s<\/td><td>passes, 533.4 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6<\/td><td>run 5 + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>a94bb636<\/code>, passive tuning PR #55)<\/td><td>passes, 45.6 s<\/td><td>passes, 492.2 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7<\/td><td>run 6 + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>92407a06<\/code>, Hunt Edict native port PR #53)<\/td><td>passes, 46.7 s<\/td><td>passes, 437.2 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8<\/td><td>run 7 + merged <code>main<\/code> (<code>b1970567<\/code>, tutorial wiring PR #56)<\/td><td>passes, 45.6 s<\/td><td>fails after 367.8 s: the run crossed midnight and the attendance window reopened (F07 step)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>9<\/td><td>same executable as run 8, after midnight<\/td><td>passes, 41.8 s<\/td><td>fails after 402.8 s: pointer missed in the F05 step<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10<\/td><td>run 9 + missed-pointer diagnostics (no behaviour change)<\/td><td>passes, 45.0 s<\/td><td>passes, 507.1 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>11<\/td><td>run 10 + <code>Tap<\/code> settling<\/td><td>passes, 44.8 s<\/td><td>passes, 446.8 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>12<\/td><td>same executable<\/td><td>passes, 41.4 s<\/td><td>passes, 539.1 s<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>13<\/td><td>same executable<\/td><td>passes, 41.2 s<\/td><td>passes, 538.5 s<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p>The second launch of run 5 passed the 10 pointer steps of the survival lesson (potion picker → <code>Extra survival supplies<\/code> → dodge group → picker → <code>Avoid all warnings<\/code> → save → close), the kill, reward and arrival dialogue, the regular first rift, F05, F06, F07 training and retry, the late-unlock briefing, the supported enhancement and the replay (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt\">all PASS sentences<\/a>). There is no error in the log. In runs 1 to 4 the per-step PASS sentences are written once at the end of the smoke, so a mid-run failure leaves none; progress there was judged from the evidence files written in order and from the failure point.<\/p><p>The second launches of runs 6 and 7 also produced the same 17 PASS sentences and have no error in the log (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run6-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt\">all of them, run 6<\/a>). The passing runs 10 to 13 produced the same 17 (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run13-runtime-tutorial-smoke.txt\">all of them, run 13<\/a>); only the hero level in the F06 sentence (3 or 4, from the natural leveling of the first rift) varies. Run 7 is the tree after the port rebuilt the window surface. The potion picker of the survival lesson, the v3 guidance of the replay, the edict notice card and the attendance handling all passed unchanged in the new window.<\/p><p>The seven related EditMode classes (<code>HuntEdictProgressionTests<\/code> 37, <code>HuntEdictQuickPresetTests<\/code> 11, <code>TutorialProgressionTests<\/code> 33, <code>TutorialChapterTests<\/code> 6, the port&#x27;s <code>HuntEdictSentenceTests<\/code> 6, and the tutorial wiring&#x27;s <code>EdictGuidanceTests<\/code> 9 and <code>PrologueGateTests<\/code> 8) passed 110 of 110 on the final tree. The first four classes also passed 87 of 87 on the code of runs 5 and 6. The added test pins <code>Quick<\/code>&#x27;s values and does not reproduce the original symptom. That symptom was a window condition, so the smoke is the check.<\/p><p>The v3 first-run acceptance smoke (<code>-hellscriptEdictProgressionSmoke<\/code>) was run because the <code>!ProgressivePrologue<\/code> condition of section 1 touches the v3 prologue window of new accounts. Before the port merge, both the fixed code and an executable built from the same files of <code>main<\/code> before the fix passed the first launch. Their second launch failed after 95 to 97 s at the same point with the same evidence, <code>A committed progression change did not reveal its tab.<\/code> (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure.txt\">fixed code<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-baseline.txt\">before<\/a>). That was a stale <code>highestClear=3<\/code> expectation after the chronicle changed the edict ladder, and PR #53 fixed it. Right after the port merge the smoke got past that point and its second launch timed out in an <code>Until<\/code> on the plaza with the daily attendance window open (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-attendance-window-after-port.png\">screen<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-failure-after-port.txt\">record<\/a>). PR #56 added the attendance hide to that smoke too, so on the final tree with the tutorial wiring merged it passes through the second launch (103.2 s, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/v3-acceptance-result.txt\">all PASS sentences<\/a>). That run includes the stretch this change touches: comparison lesson, HP lesson, boss and arrival. None of these stops was caused by this change.<\/p><p>Evidence: <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/runs.json\">run log<\/a>, failure screens of runs 1 to 3 (<a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run1-timeout-attendance-popup.png\">1<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run2-timeout-edict-notice.png\">2<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run3-timeout-replay-v3.png\">3<\/a>), the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run4-failure.txt\">run 4 failure record<\/a>, the regression screen, the survival lesson <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-04-potion-picker.png\">picker step<\/a>, <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-05-careful-choice.png\">preset choice<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/survival-step-09-save.png\">save step<\/a>, the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/first-rift-preparation.png\">rift preparation screen<\/a>, the <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/run5-replay-complete.png\">replay completion screen<\/a> and the EditMode results <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-premerge.xml\">before the merges<\/a> and <a href=\"sources/Docs/Implementation/TutorialSmokeEvidence20261005/editmode-final.xml\">final<\/a>. Executable hashes and the build and run commands are in the run log. Build and smoke outputs stay in a temporary task path; only the evidence above is kept in the repository.<\/p><h2 id=\"not-verified\">Not verified<\/h2><ul><li>The pre-fix executable was not re-run in this tree. The cause was judged from the reported failure, code analysis and the pass at the same point after the fix. Only the v3 acceptance smoke was run on pre-fix code, for the comparison above.<\/li><li>The full EditMode suite and the other smokes were not run. The shared-UI smoke (<code>-hellscriptSharedUiSmoke<\/code>), which walks every group&#x27;s picker with a legacy account, was not run either. In the window the port rebuilt, the legacy potion picker was checked only through the v2 survival lesson.<\/li><li>The cause of the <code>Tap<\/code> settling fix is inferred from the code and there is no screenshot of the failing moment. The evidence is a small sample (one failure in three attempts before, three passes in a row after), so the intermittent failure is not claimed to be gone.<\/li><li>The real screen of a new account after this change was not opened by hand. It was checked through the v3 acceptance smoke&#x27;s HP lesson and through <code>Quick<\/code> returning the same values.<\/li><li>In the smoke fixture the picker reads <code>Current settings<\/code> while the lesson line says <code>Balanced supplies<\/code>. The fixture is a hybrid account (a fresh hero under a legacy flag). It looks like the new hero&#x27;s automatic potion buying being off, which matches no preset, but that was not confirmed and it was not changed.<\/li><li>macOS synthetic pointer verification only; not a physical mobile device and not a user-comprehension test.<\/li><\/ul>", "headings": [{"id": "1-the-potion-picker-in-the-survival-lesson--app-fixed", "title": "1. The potion picker in the survival lesson — app, fixed"}, {"id": "2-the-attendance-popup--smoke-fixed", "title": "2. The attendance popup — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "3-the-edict-notice-card--smoke-fixed", "title": "3. The edict notice card — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "4-the-replay--smoke-fixed", "title": "4. The replay — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "5-window-rebuild-and-the-pointer--smoke-fixed", "title": "5. Window rebuild and the pointer — smoke, fixed"}, {"id": "verification", "title": "Verification"}, {"id": "not-verified", "title": "Not verified"}]}];
